5,Traditional Thai Music - YouTubeKra–Dai-speaking peoples - WikipediaTHE MUSICAL TRADITIONS OF NORTHEAST THAILAND,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SXXK4P2Ogs0,"Feb 14, 2009 · Traditional Thai music is a blending of musical elements from a number of cultures, such as Chinese, Khmer, and Indian. This applies not only to the instruments but also to the melodies Recent Kra-Dai migrations have brought considerable numbers of Kra-Dai peoples to Japan, Taiwan, Sri Lanka, the United Arab Emirates, Europe, Australia, New Zealand, North America and Argentina as well. The terms may have come into use as recently as 1945 when northeastern vocal music reappeared in Bangkok, and the singers used these terms for the benefit of the central Thai.","Thai, Northeastern",Kra-Dai
